# Screenshots
#
# Four things to capture - everything, one monitor, the focused window, a
# dragged region - each either saved to ~/Pictures/maim or put straight on the
# clipboard. Ctrl is the "to the clipboard instead" modifier.
#
# Plain Print is still every monitor, which on this machine is a 3840x1080
# image with two desktops in it. $mod+Shift+Print is the one screen you are
# working on: script/screenshot.sh takes the output the pointer is on, and i3
# warps the pointer onto whichever output has focus, so it is the screen you
# are looking at. `screenshot.sh monitor HDMI-1` names one from a terminal.
#
# All eight go through script/screenshot.sh, which names the file so it sorts,
# tells a cancelled selection apart from a failed capture, and shows the shot
# it just took as the notification's icon. Middle-clicking that popup opens
# the file (mouse_middle_click = do_action, in dunstrc).
bindsym Print                  exec --no-startup-id $HOME/.config/i3/script/screenshot.sh full
bindsym $mod+Shift+Print       exec --no-startup-id $HOME/.config/i3/script/screenshot.sh monitor
bindsym $mod+Print             exec --no-startup-id $HOME/.config/i3/script/screenshot.sh window
bindsym Shift+Print            exec --no-startup-id $HOME/.config/i3/script/screenshot.sh region

## Clipboard Screenshots
bindsym Ctrl+Print             exec --no-startup-id $HOME/.config/i3/script/screenshot.sh full --clip
bindsym Ctrl+$mod+Shift+Print  exec --no-startup-id $HOME/.config/i3/script/screenshot.sh monitor --clip
bindsym Ctrl+$mod+Print        exec --no-startup-id $HOME/.config/i3/script/screenshot.sh window --clip
bindsym Ctrl+Shift+Print       exec --no-startup-id $HOME/.config/i3/script/screenshot.sh region --clip

# GTK theming is settings.ini (dark Adwaita) plus the generated gtk.css, which
# repaints Adwaita's accent to match the wallpaper. Nothing to exec here - the
# old `env GTK_THEME=...` line set a variable in a shell that exited
# immediately, so it never reached a single GTK app.

# Lock screen: the wallpaper with the generated palette on the indicator.
#
# This was commented out and pointed at a path the script has never been at -
# it lives under script/ with everything else - so there was no lock key at
# all. Ctrl rather than Shift because hjkl keeps all four of both rows:
# $mod+hjkl focuses, $mod+Shift+hjkl moves.
# Locking before suspend is wired to xss-lock further up.
bindsym $mod+Ctrl+l exec --no-startup-id $HOME/.config/i3/script/i3lock-color.sh

# i3-gaps
gaps inner 1
gaps outer 0
